    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/055E28882001FE667534B0880CFCD275/jobs/98706": {
      "title": "Head Women's Softball Coach",
      "description": "Head Women's Softball Coach You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Head Women's Softball Coach Hot Job Jersey City, NJ 07306 Apply Overview Salary Range $51,000.00 - $53,000.00 Salary/year Position Type Full Time Apply Description About Saint Peter’s University Saint Peter’s is one of 27 Jesuit colleges and universities in the United States. Established in 1872, the University blends a unique learning experience shaped by rigorous academics, internships that provide real-world experience, community service, and a genuine, caring community that supports alumni long after graduation. Saint Peter’s offers more than 50 undergraduate majors as well as master’s level and doctorate program. Saint Peter’s University’s diverse campus community, collegial and inclusive culture, and commitment to excellence, education, innovation and community engagement contribute to our success and ensures our employees flourish. The University merges quality academics, distinguished and exceptional faculty and staff, and modern facilities to engage and challenge its 4,000 students who share in the desire to shape the future through insight, intellectual exploration, discernment, and community service and engagement. Position Title and Job Summary: The Head Women’s Softball Coach is responsible for organizing and directing all aspects of the women’s softball program. This individual must demonstrate the ability to lead a program with longstanding tradition of excellence in both athletics and academics by preparing its student-athletes of assuming roles of leadership and service in their future.  This is a full-time position. Job Duties and Responsibilities: Administer all phases of an NCAA Division I women’s softball program. Develop and supervise the student-athletes in the women’s softball program, by implementing strategies to motivate maximum levels of individual and team performance. Recruit and retain academically and athletically qualified student-athletes, working directly with the Admissions Department. Monitor student-athletes academic progress. Promote a philosophy of educational welfare, sportsmanship and conduct in alignment with the University’s mission. Schedule non-conference games in competitive season. Create long term player development including technical, tactical and physical development of individual players. Organize, prepare and supervise all training practices and game day contests. Have direct contact with Residence Life for student-athlete housing and needs. Responsible for placing orders for all equipment and gear needed for the season with Equipment Manager. To be finalized with the Sr. Associate AD for Business and Finance. Coordinate all travel with the Sr. Associate AD for Business and Finance. Maintain responsibility for budget control by adhering to operational budgets. Hire, supervise and assign responsibilities of assistant coaches. Undertake public relations and promotional activities appropriate to the position to promote the women’s softball team. Adhere to all MAAC and NCAA rules and regulations Any other duty or responsibility assigned by the supervisor Salary Range: $51,000 - $53,000 Benefits: Along with a competitive salary, we provide a robust benefits package to support your health and future goals. Key Benefits Include: Paid Time Off: Paid holidays, personal days, vacation, and sick leave Health Coverage: Health insurance, dental insurance, and vision insurance Life Insurance: Employer-provided life insurance Life & Disability Insurance: Voluntary life and voluntary disability coverage Retirement Savings: 401(k) plan with Roth and Traditional options Tuition Remission: An attractive tuition remission policy for employees and their dependents Additional Perks: Employee Assistance Program (EAP), Voluntary Legal plan, FSA and more The well-being of our employees is a priority for our University, and we are committed to promoting your success and well-being. Qualifications Required Qualifications: Commitment and sensitivity to the needs and dynamics of a culturally diverse student body that includes a large percentage of first generation and low-income students. Creative, innovative and self-motivated individual with the ability to work creatively in an atmosphere of limited resources. Commitment and sensitivity to the Jesuit and Catholic ideals that form the mission of Saint Peter’s University; and willingness to integrate these ideals into all aspects of the Athletics Department. Organizational, communication, and interpersonal skills. Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a dynamic environment. Commitment to community engagement, service, leadership development, or related work. Preferred Qualifications: Experience developing and maintaining community partnerships. Experience working directly with community-based organizations. Familiarity with service-learning, civic engagement, volunteer management, or leadership development programs. Education: Bachelor’s degree required. Preferred a minimum of five years successful coaching experience in softball at the college or professional level. Knowledge of MAAC and NCAA rules and regulations for compliance.  Public relations skills; excellent interpersonal and communications skills; and excellent organizational skills. Have the ability to deal with students, faculty, staff, alumni, boosters, college administrations and all media outlets. Experience: Preferred a minimum of five years successful coaching experience in softball at the college or professional level Licenses: Must have a valid driver’s license in good standing. Physical Requirements: Must be able to physically teach workouts and plays for a softball team. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/055E28882001FE667534B0880CFCD275/jobs/99070": {
      "title": "Assistant Women's Basketball Coach Part-time",
      "description": "Assistant Women's Basketball Coach Part-time You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Assistant Women's Basketball Coach Part-time Hot Job Jersey City, NJ 07306 Apply Overview Salary Range $15.92 - $16.39 Hourly Position Type Part Time Apply Description About Saint Peter’s University Saint Peter’s is one of 27 Jesuit colleges and universities in the United States. Established in 1872, the University blends a unique learning experience shaped by rigorous academics, internships that provide real-world experience, community service, and a genuine, caring community that supports alumni long after graduation. Saint Peter’s offers more than 50 undergraduate majors as well as master’s level and doctorate program. Saint Peter’s University’s diverse campus community, collegial and inclusive culture, and commitment to excellence, education, innovation and community engagement contribute to our success and ensures our employees flourish. The University merges quality academics, distinguished and exceptional faculty and staff, and modern facilities to engage and challenge its 4,000 students who share in the desire to shape the future through insight, intellectual exploration, discernment, and community service and engagement. Job Summary: The Assistant Women’s Basketball Coach is responsible for assisting all aspects of the women’s basketball program. Duties and Responsibilities: Assist in the administration of all phases of an NCAA Division I women’s basketball program. Help develop and supervise the student-athletes in the women’s basketball program, by supporting the head coach’s strategies to motivate maximum levels of individual and team performance. Assist in recruiting and retaining academically and athletically qualified student-athletes, working directly with the Admissions Department. Along with the head coach, monitor student-athletes academic progress. Support the head coach in promoting a philosophy of educational welfare, sportsmanship and conduct in alignment with the University’s mission. Assist in organizing, preparing and supervising all training practices and game day contests. Assist in ordering of athletic gear. Assist in coordinating all travel. Assist in the positive promotion of the women’s basketball team. Adhere to all MAAC and NCAA rules and regulations. Any other duty or responsibility assigned by the supervisor. Hourly Rate: $15.92 - $16.39 Qualifications Required Qualifications: Commitment and sensitivity to the needs and dynamics of a culturally diverse student body that includes a large percentage of first generation and low income students. Creative, innovative and self-motivated individual with the ability to work creatively in an atmosphere of limited resources. Commitment and sensitivity to the Jesuit and Catholic ideals that form the mission of Saint Peter’s University; and willingness to integrate these ideals into all aspects of the Athletics Department. Reports directly to the Head Women’s Basketball Coach. 50% instruct, teach and assist in the development of players during practices.  Follow and conform to NCAA rules and regulations. Organizational, communication, and interpersonal skills. Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a dynamic environment. Commitment to community engagement, service, leadership development, or related work. Preferred Qualifications: Experience developing and maintaining community partnerships. Experience working directly with community-based organizations. Familiarity with service-learning, civic engagement, volunteer management, or leadership development programs. Education: Bachelor’s degree required. Preferred competitive coaching experience in women’s soccer at the high school or college level.  Knowledge of MAAC and NCAA rules and regulations for compliance.  Have the ability to work with students, faculty, staff, alumni, boosters, college administrators. Video and computer experience preferred (Synergy). Licenses: Must have a valid driver’s license in good standing. Physical requirements: Must be able to sustain workouts and practice for hours several times a week with the team. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/055E28882001FE667534B0880CFCD275/jobs/99309": {
      "title": "Transfer Admissions Counselor",
      "description": "Transfer Admissions Counselor You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Transfer Admissions Counselor Hot Job Jersey City, NJ 07306 Apply Overview Salary Range $24.72 - $27.47 Hourly Position Type Full Time Apply Description About Saint Peter’s University Saint Peter’s is one of 27 Jesuit colleges and universities in the United States. Established in 1872, the University blends a unique learning experience shaped by rigorous academics, internships that provide real-world experience, community service, and a genuine, caring community that supports alumni long after graduation. Saint Peter’s offers more than 50 undergraduate majors as well as master’s level and doctorate program. Saint Peter’s University’s diverse campus community, collegial and inclusive culture, and commitment to excellence, education, innovation and community engagement contribute to our success and ensures our employees flourish. The University merges quality academics, distinguished and exceptional faculty and staff, and modern facilities to engage and challenge its 4,000 students who share in the desire to shape the future through insight, intellectual exploration, discernment, and community service and engagement. Job Summary: Reporting to the Director of Undergraduate Admissions, the Transfer Admissions Counselor represents the University to prospective transfer students, returning students, their families, community college counselors, academic advisors, and other college-access partners in a variety of on- and off-campus settings. The Transfer Admissions Counselor is responsible for the recruitment, admission, re-enrollment, and enrollment of prospective transfer and returning students, developing relationships with community colleges and other transfer partners, and guiding students through the admissions process from initial inquiry through enrollment. Supervisory Responsibility: This position has no direct reports. Outcomes / Performance Measures: Primary Duties: Serve as the primary contact for prospective transfer and re-enrolling students, providing individualized guidance through the admissions and enrollment process, including application completion, transcript review, and next steps toward registration. Provides transfer evaluations of transcripts and documentation in accordance with institutional policies. Work with academic departments, CASE and enrollment services offices to ensure accurate evaluation and placement of transfer credits. Lead outreach efforts to assist former students seeking re-admission, providing advice and support to facilitate their successful return and degree completion. Conduct proactive outreach to prospective students through phone calls, email, text messaging, virtual appointments, events, and other recruitment initiatives. Remains current on University programs and offerings to ensure accurate and up to date information is being provided to prospective students and other members of the community. Processes the application-related materials and corresponding student records in Slate and Colleague in a time-sensitive manner with accuracy and a strong attention to detail, and facilitates the timely completion of applications. Participate in and represent the University at transfer fairs, community college visits, college nights, open houses, information sessions, admitted student events, and other recruitment programs. Utilizes a variety of software programs including but not limited to Colleague, Slate, Outlook, Word, Excel, Zoom and other related programs. Performs other duties as assigned. Any other duty or responsibility assigned by the supervisor. Hourly Range: $24.72 - $27.47 Benefits: Along with a competitive salary, we provide a robust benefits package to support your health and future goals. Key Benefits Include: Paid Time Off: Paid holidays, personal days, vacation, and sick leave Health Coverage: Health insurance, dental insurance, and vision insurance Life Insurance: Employer-provided life insurance Life & Disability Insurance: Voluntary life and voluntary disability coverage Retirement Savings: 401(k) plan with Roth and Traditional options Tuition Remission: An attractive tuition remission policy for employees and their dependents Additional Perks: Employee Assistance Program (EAP), Voluntary Legal plan, FSA and more The well-being of our employees is a priority for our University, and we are committed to promoting your success and well-being. Qualifications Required Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree required Strong organizational skills, with an attention to detail and ability to process critical information in a timely manner. Strong interpersonal and communication skills with a student-centered approach Experience working within a CRM (Slate) and Student Information System (Colleague) Experience in a higher education setting, preferably in an academic setting or advisement, Ability to manage multiple priorities and meet deadlines in a fast-paced environment Availability to occasionally work outside of normal hours, evenings and/or weekends in the performance of assigned responsibilities. Ability to travel when needed (minimal and within state). Valid driver’s license required Organizational, communication, and interpersonal skills. Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a dynamic environment. Commitment to community engagement, service, leadership development, or related work. Preferred Qualifications: Experience developing and maintaining community partnerships. Experience working directly with community-based organizations. Familiarity with service-learning, civic engagement, volunteer management, or leadership development programs. Work Schedule: Full-time; In addition to regular business hours, the person in this position must be able to be flexible around the needs of the University, which includes occasional evening and/or weekend hours. Disclaimer: This job description is intended to summarize the type and level of work performed by the incumbent and is not an exhaustive list of duties, responsibilities, and requirements. The University reserves the right to change, add, or reassign job duties or combine positions, or portions thereof, at any time. This job description is not an employment agreement or contract. This job description may be updated from time to time based on the needs of the University. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    }
  },
